      "id": "document:src/engines/SessionCore/ARCHITECTURE.md",
      "type": "document",
      "name": "ARCHITECTURE.md",
      "filePath": "src/engines/SessionCore/ARCHITECTURE.md",
      "summary": "Deep-dive architecture doc for the SessionCore engine covering the session event pipeline (sync layer to Rust ingestion to core atoms to rendering), canonical name resolution, key files per layer, and the simulator rendering architecture.",
      "tags": ["documentation", "architecture", "session-core", "event-pipeline"],
      "complexity": "complex",
      "languageNotes": "Documents a deliberate TS/Rust split where all chunk normalization runs in Rust (src-tauri/src/event_store/ingestion/) and the TypeScript layer only calls Tauri IPC."
    },
    {
      "id": "file:src/engines/SessionCore/control/optimisticTurnStatus.ts",
      "type": "file",
      "name": "optimisticTurnStatus.ts",
      "filePath": "src/engines/SessionCore/control/optimisticTurnStatus.ts",
      "summary": "Tracks a short-lived \"optimistically started\" marker per session so the UI can bridge the gap between a user sending a turn and the backend confirming it started.",
      "tags": ["state-management", "session", "optimistic-update", "utility"],
      "complexity": "moderate"
    },
    {
      "id": "file:src/engines/SessionCore/control/turnLifecycle.ts",
      "type": "file",
      "name": "turnLifecycle.ts",
      "filePath": "src/engines/SessionCore/control/turnLifecycle.ts",
      "summary": "Per-session turn lifecycle state machine (idle to dispatching to running to stopping to terminal) with a deadman-timer safeguard that force-idles stuck turns and a signal atom for reactive consumers.",
      "tags": ["state-management", "session", "lifecycle", "state-machine"],
      "complexity": "complex",
      "languageNotes": "Uses a deadman-timer pattern: each phase transition arms a timeout that force-resets the turn to idle if no follow-up transition arrives, guarding against turns that get stuck mid-flight."
    },
